[#:seon.task{:name "a-development-cluster-boots-in-tens-of-seconds"
  :kind :function
  :intent "`seon.sci.eval-instrumentation-test/an-instrumented-dev-cluster-builds-an-attempt-ready-prompt` boots one real development cluster with `seon.cluster.boot/start!` and ran 49.9 s (declared bound 5 s; throwaway JVM check on 7a9ceb44a with two other test runs running). Over ten seconds needs an issue: profile start! on an empty store, name the armed functions that dominate and fix them. Done when the same test measures under its declared bound."
  :must-read #{seon.cluster.boot/start!}
  :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/review/red-triage.md"}}

 #:seon.task{:name "reset-cli-stdout-is-not-one-edn-value"
  :kind :function
  :intent "`seon.cluster.boot-test/reset-one-jvm` errors on HEAD a6231e1ad (throwaway test run, 2026-10-08): its `bin/seon --root R reset --force` child's stdout begins with an ISO timestamp (`Invalid number: 2026-10-08T11:06:39.608Z` from `clojure.edn/read-string` in the test's `completed!`), so the reset reply is no longer one EDN value on stdout. Find the producer of the timestamped line on the operator's stdout and send it to stderr or the start log, or make the reply the one value; the test is the proof."
  :must-read #{seon.cluster.boot/request! seon.operator/request!}}

 #:seon.task{:name "request-failure-message-is-a-printed-cause-chain"
  :kind :function
  :intent "`seon.cluster.boot/request!`'s catch builds an unrefused failure's `:seon.error/message` from `seon.render.value/core-text` of the cause: the message is a printed vector of the whole cause chain (ex-data, problems, frames), so `bin/seon status` and the operator log show a multi-kilobyte string instead of short fixed text with the cause's members as data. Seen 2026-10-09 when `seon.cluster.boot/readiness` refused an instance row. Done when the message is the cause's own `:seon.error/message` (or short fixed text) and the cause's error map rides as data."
  :must-read #{seon.cluster.boot/request! seon.cluster.boot/diagnostic seon.render.value/core-text}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-paused-boot-arms-every-open-attempt-and-runs-nothing"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Card R3. `start --paused` writes `:seon.cluster/execution :paused` before the reconciler's prime, so every open attempt's graph exists and answers ping while no transform, proof or model call runs; an ordinary start re-hosts open attempts on their branches from their rows (today an assigned branch agent is not re-hosted after a restart)."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.boot/start! seon.cluster/start-flows! seon.cluster/recover-runs!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/runtime-follows-db.md"}}]
